  startDayButton: {fileID: 1994809142}
  dialogue: {fileID: 353443300}
  dialogueLines:
  - "Good morning, dear! So Yusuf\u2019s workshop is open again. I brought you something...\nThis
    was my husband\u2019s radio. We listened to the fishing news on it every evening."
  - 'It went quiet last winter. The dial glass cracked and a wire came loose inside.

    Yusuf
    always said nothing is too old to be fixed. Will you try?'
  headOutLine: Before you head out, dear... would you take a look at my radio?
  charsPerSecond: 55
  tellMoreButton: {fileID: 2128087521}
  letsFixButton: {fileID: 780546982}
  tasksButtonActive: {fileID: 773694021}
  tasksPanel: {fileID: 993226564}
  panelSlide: 860
  taskCount: {fileID: 883866955}
  taskBadge: {fileID: 177551315}
  meetCheck: {fileID: 1194620995}
  meetStrike: {fileID: 1103786795}
  meetFade: {fileID: 1648132273}
  meetStrikeWidth: 300
  repairCheck: {fileID: 676029531}
  repairStrike: {fileID: 253831979}
  repairFade: {fileID: 390496872}
  repairStrikeWidth: 266
  repair: {fileID: 798798896}
  tasksTotal: 5
  afterRepairLines:
  - Ooh! Is that... the fishing news? Just like my late husband and I listened to
    every evening! Bless your hands, dear. Yusuf would be proud of you.
  - In our day, nothing got thrown away so easily. We fixed what broke and reused
    what was old. Now everything goes straight in the bin, and most of that bin ends
    up in the sea.
  - 'You fixed this radio with things you collected from the sea. That''s recycling:
    a bottle became glass, a net became rope, and this old radio spoke again.'
  - 'Here, take this, you''ve earned it. Tonight I''ll tell the whole town on this
    radio: switch off the lights by the shore at night, the turtles are coming!'
